# Editor state. The Swift extension for VS Code writes launch configurations
# for the bare SwiftPM executables, which is exactly the launch path README.md
# tells people not to use; Scripts/bundle-app.sh is the supported one.
.vscode/

# The centering tool (D-11 / TICKET-034). It lives here for convenience and
# must never reach GitHub: this repository has a live public remote, so a
# stray commit is one push from publishing it. The pre-commit guard in
# .githooks/ is the other half — this line handles the ordinary commit, the
# guard handles the one hurried `git add -f` on a day nobody is thinking
# about it.
centering/

# Internal working documents. They stay on the operator's machine because they
# are a private engineering diary rather than product documentation: the ticket
# queue records commercial rationale, real batch and consignor names, the
# destination Drive folder, and third-party integration detail that is nobody
# else's to publish. SPEC.md is the public contract; CONTRIBUTING.md is the
# public working agreement. Those two are what a contributor actually needs.
CLAUDE.md
PENDINGTICKETS.md

# A dense, page-cited distillation of PFU's copyrighted 644-page user guide.
# The individual facts are functional and uncopyrightable, but the selection and
# arrangement are a derivative of one source, and nothing in ScanDeck needs it
# published to be useful.
docs/research/paperstream-capture-inventory.md

# The broader UX study of a general-purpose PaperStream Capture remake. It is
# local research, not part of the product: it uses PFU's trademark as the
# working name of the proposed app — in its title, in draft error copy, in a
# menu item and in a wireframe's title bar — which is branding use rather than
# the nominative use everything else in this repository sticks to. ScanDeck is
# not that app and never was, so publishing it would put someone else's mark on
# a product surface for no benefit. Kept locally as a UX quality bar.
PaperStream_for_Mac_UI_Spec_v1.0.docx.md
